<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">promotion</ansi>

Promotion is how a character picks its class. It is permanent, and it is the
biggest choice a character makes after its archetype.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">When</ansi>

  Level 10   an advanced class, on the good, neutral or evil route
  Level 30   an elite class, where your route has one (Hierarch, Demonologist,
             Elder Druid, Paladin, Warlord, Dread Knight, Pathfinder, Swordmaster,
             Nightblade, Sentinel, Marksman, Ravager); see <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">class paths</ansi>                     what each route of your lineage offers and asks
  <ansi fg="command">class promote [class]</ansi>           preview a promotion: its ranks, its gate
  <ansi fg="command">class promote [class] confirm</ansi>   make it

For a companion, add its name: <ansi fg="command">class promote tamsin priest confirm</ansi>. A companion
promotes on its own record: the leader chooses, and the choice is saved with
the company.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The alignment gate</ansi>

Good routes need alignment +30 or higher and evil routes -30 or lower when
you promote. Neutral routes need nothing, and the Samurai (Kensai,
Hatamoto, Ronin) and Shaman (Stormcaller, Mistweaver, Earthspeaker) lineages
have only neutral routes. If your alignment is not yet right,
<ansi fg="command">class</ansi> says the promotion is waiting; you keep your ranks and promote once your
alignment recovers (see <ansi fg="command">help alignment</ansi>). A class is never lowered.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What you get</ansi>

Elite classes ask the same gate when you promote, and a character that never
took the advanced class can take both steps in one visit. A promotion starts the class's ranks at once, including every rank your level
has already reached. Spells those ranks teach are learned immediately. A class
changes how you fight but never takes anything away.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help rogue-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ranger-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cleric-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help warrior-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help dollmaster-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help beasttamer-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>.
